MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset="utf-8"
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

I think the problem is the following: effectplot uses multiple
imputation,
with the results of the function sim.geno.  The find.pseudomarker
function
can look for pseudomarker locations either in those results (by using
where="draws") or in the genotype probabilities calculated via
calc.genoprob
(by using where="prob").

So it is important to use where="draws" in find.pseudomarker if you are
going to subsequently use the pseudomarker name in effectplot.

karl
